    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d538-a8">

                <pb facs="0892" n="756" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg756"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 8 in No.
                    973.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Becker to Mr.
                            Blacklock.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >German Consulate</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Apia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1888-09-09"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">September</hi> 9,
                    1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I hereby notify the consulate of the United States that in consequence of the
                    appearance of armed mobs in the vicinity of Apia I am compelled to ask the
                    commander of the I. M. Krz. <hi rendition="#italic">Adler</hi> to send a
                    detachment of soldiers to Apia for the protection of German property and
                    others.</p>
                <p>Therefore has the said commander, with permission of Samoan Government, posted a
                    guard on the boundaries of Sogi and Mulinuu.</p>
                <p>The United States consulate I hereby notify to acquaint the American citizens
                    with the above.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Becker</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Imperial German
                    Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
